# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Agent Forge — environment template
# Copy to `.env.local` (gitignored) and fill in a key for one provider.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Which provider Forge uses to BUILD and RUN agents: "anthropic" or "openai".
# Overridable per-command with --provider.
LLM_PROVIDER=anthropic

# Provide the key for whichever provider you select (both is fine).
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=sk-ant-...
# OPENAI_API_KEY=sk-...

# Optional model overrides (defaults: claude-fable-5 / gpt-4.1)
# ANTHROPIC_MODEL=claude-fable-5
# OPENAI_MODEL=gpt-4.1

# ---- Slack bot (npm run slack) — "message your minions" ----
# Socket Mode, so no public URL is needed. See the README for how to get these.
# SLACK_BOT_TOKEN=xoxb-...
# SLACK_APP_TOKEN=xapp-...
# Optional: a default repo so you can say "fix issue 3" without naming it.
# MINION_DEFAULT_REPO=salehaiftikharr/forge-minions-demo

# ---- Linear (optional) — work off Linear issues, e.g. "fix ENG-123 in owner/repo" ----
# Linear → Settings → API → Personal API keys.
# LINEAR_API_KEY=lin_api_...

# ---- Test runner (optional) ----
# Minions auto-detect how a repo runs its tests (vitest, jest, mocha, go,
# node:test, or an npm "test" script). Set these only to force a command for a
# repo that isn't detected — no code change needed to point minions elsewhere.
# MINION_TEST_CMD=make test
# MINION_TEST_FORMAT=tap   # tap | jest | go | exit  (how to read the output)

# ---- Gate hardening (optional) ----
# Run the suite N times and only trust a test that passes EVERY run, so a flaky
# green never earns a ship (default 1; 3 is cheap insurance on flaky repos).
# MINION_TEST_RUNS=3
# Mutation testing: after a fix goes green, perturb its lines and re-run; if the
# test survives every mutation the fix is likely gamed. Max mutants per run
# (default 6; set 0 to disable).
# MINION_MUTANTS=6

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Functional application (npm run migrate / npm run worker + the web tier)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The worker is the ONLY tier that talks to a model provider. For a live
# deployment set LLM_PROVIDER=anthropic (or openai) and supply the key above.
# For an offline/CI/local proof set LLM_PROVIDER=fake — the full engine runs
# deterministically on the practice repo with no network and no key.

# Shared SQLite database. The web tier and the worker MUST point at the same
# file. Default: ./.forge-data/forge.db relative to the working directory.
# On a deployed worker, put this on a PERSISTENT disk.
# FORGE_DB_PATH=/data/forge.db

# The practice repo the minion works on, and where per-run workspaces are copied.
# Defaults are fine locally; set absolute paths on a worker with a persistent disk.
# FORGE_SEED_DIR=./sandbox
# FORGE_RUNS_DIR=./.forge-data/runs

# Worker tuning (optional).
# FORGE_LEASE_MS=60000   # job lease; an expired lease is reclaimed on recovery
# FORGE_POLL_MS=1000     # how often the worker polls for new work

# ---- GitHub coding runs (docs/functional/CONNECTIONS.md) ----
# fake (default, offline, no repo touched) | real (clones + opens a real draft PR)
# FORGE_GITHUB=fake
# real mode needs GitHub auth on the worker: `gh auth login` (local) or a GitHub App.

# ---- Shared-engine Slack bot (npm run slack:app) ----
# Uses the SAME FORGE_DB_PATH as the worker and web. Socket Mode (no public URL).
# SLACK_BOT_TOKEN=xoxb-...
# SLACK_APP_TOKEN=xapp-...
# FORGE_WEB_URL=https://your-web-host      # used in Slack run links
# FORGE_SLACK_APPROVERS=U0123,U0456         # optional: Slack user ids allowed to approve
# FORGE_SLACK_POLL_MS=2000                  # milestone poll interval
